        <p>The <b>Department of Surgery at IRPGIMSR &amp; associated Northern Railways Central Hospital</b> under <b>Delhi University</b> is running <b>Postgraduate (NBE-MS) DNB Surgery</b> since 1991 &amp; <b>FNB Minimal Access Surgery</b> since 2022.</p>

        <p><b>Department of General Surgery</b> has demonstrated outstanding performance through its unwavering commitment to patient care, clinical excellence, academic advancement, and teamwork…</p>

       
        <div id="ntext" style="font-family:tahoma;font-size:12px; color:black">
<p align="justify"></p><div id="ViEtDeVdIvId" style="POSITION:Relative;FONT-FAMILY:Arial;FONT-SIZE:12px; BACKGROUND-COLOR:white"><div style=""><p style=""><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana">The <b style="">Department of Surgery at IRPGIMSR &amp; associated Northern Railways Central Hospital</b> under <b style="">Delhi University</b> running <b style="">Postgraduate (NBE-MS) DNB Surgery</b> seats since 1991 &amp; <b style="">FNB Minimal Access surgery</b> since 2022.&nbsp;</font></p><p style=""><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana"><b style="">Department of General Surgery</b> has demonstrated outstanding performance through its unwavering commitment to patient care, clinical excellence, academic advancement, and teamwork. Under the guidance of dedicated faculty and resident surgeons, the Integrated department of general Surgery continues to deliver high-quality all type of surgical services across general and super-specialty fields including Advance Minimal Access Surgery, Surgical gastroenterology, Hepato-Pancreato-Biliary, Urology, Plastic Surgery, Pediatric Surgery, Neurosurgery, Breast and Endocrine Surgery, Vascular Surgery, Coloproctology, and Surgical Oncology.<o:p></o:p></font></p> <p style=""><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana">Over the past year, the department has significantly enhanced surgical outcomes through meticulous preoperative evaluation, evidence-based operative techniques, and compassionate postoperative care. The successful conduct of complex and emergency surgeries, combined with the introduction of minimally invasive and advanced laparoscopic procedures, reflects the department's pursuit of innovation and excellence.<o:p></o:p></font></p> <p style=""><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana">Academic activities have remained strong, with regular case presentations, clinical audits, morbidity-mortality meetings, and participation in national conferences. The team's contribution to research and publications has further elevated the institution's reputation.<o:p></o:p></font></p> <p style=""><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana">The department's exemplary coordination with anaesthesia, radiology, and critical care units ensures seamless multidisciplinary management. Its dedication to patient safety, ethical practice, and continuous learning embodies the true spirit of service in a government hospital setting.<o:p></o:p></font></p> <p style=""><b><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana"><u>Gastrointestinal , Hepato-Pancreato-Biliary (HPB) and Minimal Access Surgery</u></font></b></p><p style=""><b><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana"><u><img src="https://nr.indianrailways.gov.in//uploads/images/1761043135962-0a87aca8-6700-41e8-a1c9-155cbda9a9e1.jpg"><br></u></font></b></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: normal;"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana">The GI surgery unit undertakes a wide range of procedures involving the <b>esophagus, stomach, small and large intestines</b>, and <b>anorectal region</b>. Commonly performed surgeries include:<o:p></o:p></font></p> <ul type="disc" style=""> <li class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;      line-height:normal;mso-list:l2 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:list 36.0pt"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana"><b>Laparoscopic cholecystectomy</b><o:p></o:p></font></li> <li class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;      line-height:normal;mso-list:l2 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:list 36.0pt"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana"><b>Laparoscopic Appendectomy</b><o:p></o:p></font></li> <li class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;      line-height:normal;mso-list:l2 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:list 36.0pt"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana"><b>Hernia repairs (open, laparoscopic TEP/TAPP)</b><o:p></o:p></font></li> <li class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;      line-height:normal;mso-list:l2 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:list 36.0pt"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana"><b>Gastrojejunostomy, colectomy hemicolectomy,      and anterior resection</b><o:p></o:p></font></li> <li class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;      line-height:normal;mso-list:l2 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:list 36.0pt"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana"><b>Small bowel resection and anastomosis</b><o:p></o:p></font></li> <li class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;      line-height:normal;mso-list:l2 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:list 36.0pt"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana"><b>Surgery for intestinal obstruction and      perforation peritonitis</b><o:p></o:p></font></li> <li class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;      line-height:normal;mso-list:l2 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:list 36.0pt"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana"><b>Diagnostic and therapeutic laparoscopy</b><o:p></o:p></font></li> <li class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;      line-height:normal;mso-list:l2 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:list 36.0pt"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana"><b>Lap /open splenectomy</b><o:p></o:p></font></li> <li class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;      line-height:normal;mso-list:l2 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:list 36.0pt"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana"><b>Total video-scopic and laparoscopic radical      Esophagectomy for Esophageal cancers</b><o:p></o:p></font></li> <li class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;      line-height:normal;mso-list:l2 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:list 36.0pt"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana"><b>Lap /open Heller's myotomy</b><o:p></o:p></font></li> <li class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;      line-height:normal;mso-list:l2 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:list 36.0pt"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana"><b>Lap nissen's fundoplication</b><o:p></o:p></font></li> <li class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;      line-height:normal;mso-list:l2 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:list 36.0pt"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana"><b>Lap /open total Radical gastrectomy and Distal      gastrectomy</b><o:p></o:p></font></li> <li class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;      line-height:normal;mso-list:l2 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:list 36.0pt"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana"><b>Lap /open Whipple surgery</b><o:p></o:p></font></li> <li class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;      line-height:normal;mso-list:l2 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:list 36.0pt"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana"><b>Lap /open radical cholecystectomy</b><o:p></o:p></font></li> <li class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;      line-height:normal;mso-list:l2 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:list 36.0pt"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana"><b>Lap /open anterior resection and Lap APR</b><o:p></o:p></font></li> <li class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;      line-height:normal;mso-list:l2 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:list 36.0pt"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana"><b>Lap /open Total Colectomy</b></font></li><li class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;      line-height:normal;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo2;tab-stops:list 36.0pt"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana"><b>Common bile duct exploration and      choledocholithotomy</b> <o:p></o:p></font></li> <li class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;      line-height:normal;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo2;tab-stops:list 36.0pt"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana"><b>Biliary bypass and hepaticojejunostomy</b> <o:p></o:p></font></li> <li class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;      line-height:normal;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo2;tab-stops:list 36.0pt"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana"><b>Liver abscess drainage (surgical and      image-guided)</b><o:p></o:p></font></li> <li class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;      line-height:normal;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo2;tab-stops:list 36.0pt"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana"><b>Lap /open Pancreatic necro-sectomy and Lap      /open cystogastrostomy</b> <o:p></o:p></font></li> <li class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;      line-height:normal;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo2;tab-stops:list 36.0pt"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana"><b>Lap /open Distal pancreatectomy </b><o:p></o:p></font></li></ul> <p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: normal;"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana">Emergency and elective GI procedures are performed routinely, ensuring prompt surgical intervention and optimal postoperative outcomes. Minimally invasive techniques are increasingly being adopted to reduce morbidity and hospital stay.<o:p></o:p></font></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: normal;"><b><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana"><u>Academic and Clinical Excellence</u><o:p></o:p></font></b></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: normal;"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana">The unit emphasizes evidence-based management, multidisciplinary collaboration with radiology and gastroenterology, and a strong focus on patient safety. Regular <b>GI and HPB surgery case discussions</b>, <b>mortality-morbidity audits</b>, and <b>continuing surgical education sessions</b> ensure continuous quality improvement.<o:p></o:p></font></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: normal;"><b><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana"><u>Thoracic procedures</u></font></b></p> <ul><li><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana"><span style="line-height: 107%;"></span><!--[endif]--><b><span style="line-height: 107%;">VATS / Open Lobectomy<o:p></o:p></span></b></font></li><li><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana"><span style="line-height: 107%;"></span><!--[endif]--><b><span style="line-height: 107%;">VATS / Open Pneumonectomy<o:p></o:p></span></b></font></li><li><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana"><span style="line-height: 107%;"></span><!--[endif]--><b><span style="line-height: 107%;">VATS / Open Decortication<o:p></o:p></span></b></font></li><li><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana"><span style="line-height: 107%;"></span><!--[endif]--><b><span style="line-height: 107%;">Diagnostic VATS<o:p></o:p></span></b></font></li><li><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana"><span style="line-height: 107%;"></span><!--[endif]--><b><span style="line-height: 107%;">VATS Esophagectomy<o:p></o:p></span></b></font></li></ul><!--[if !supportLists]-->         <p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpLast" style=""><b><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana"><u>Urology Procedures</u></font></b></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: normal;"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana">A wide spectrum of endoscopic surgeries is routinely performed, including:<o:p></o:p></font></p> <ul type="disc" style=""> <li class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;      line-height:normal;mso-list:l5 level1 lfo3;tab-stops:list 36.0pt"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana"><b>Transurethral Resection of Prostate (TURP)</b> for benign prostatic hyperplasia (BPH)<o:p></o:p></font></li> <li class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;      line-height:normal;mso-list:l5 level1 lfo3;tab-stops:list 36.0pt"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana"><b>Transurethral Resection of Bladder Tumour      (TURBT)</b> for bladder      neoplasms<o:p></o:p></font></li> <li class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;      line-height:normal;mso-list:l5 level1 lfo3;tab-stops:list 36.0pt"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana"><b>Ureteroscopic stone removal (URS)</b> and <b>Percutaneous Nephrolithotomy (PCNL)</b>     for upper urinary tract calculi<o:p></o:p></font></li> <li class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;      line-height:normal;mso-list:l5 level1 lfo3;tab-stops:list 36.0pt"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana"><b>Cysto-lithotripsy and cysto-litholapaxy</b> for bladder stones<o:p></o:p></font></li> <li class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;      line-height:normal;mso-list:l5 level1 lfo3;tab-stops:list 36.0pt"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana"><b>Optical internal urethrotomy (OIU)</b> for urethral stricture disease<o:p></o:p></font></li></ul> <p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: normal;"><b><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana"><u>Minimally Invasive and Advanced Procedures</u><o:p></o:p></font></b></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: normal;"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana">The hospital has adopted newer and less invasive technologies to improve patient outcomes, such as:<o:p></o:p></font></p> <ul type="disc" style=""> <li class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;      line-height:normal;mso-list:l4 level1 lfo4;tab-stops:list 36.0pt"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana"><b>Laser prostatectomy</b> and <b>Rezum therapy</b> for BPH management<o:p></o:p></font></li> <li class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;      line-height:normal;mso-list:l4 level1 lfo4;tab-stops:list 36.0pt"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana"><b>Laparoscopic nephrectomy</b>, <b>pyeloplasty</b>, and <b>uretero-lithotomy</b><o:p></o:p></font></li> <li class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;      line-height:normal;mso-list:l4 level1 lfo4;tab-stops:list 36.0pt"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana"><b>Retrograde Intrarenal Surgery (RIRS)</b> for renal calculi<o:p></o:p></font></li> <li class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;      line-height:normal;mso-list:l4 level1 lfo4;tab-stops:list 36.0pt"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana"><b>Urethroplasty</b> and reconstructive surgeries for complex      urethral strictures<o:p></o:p></font></li></ul> <p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: normal;"><b><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana"><u>Oncological and Reconstructive Urology</u><o:p></o:p></font></b></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: normal;"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana">The department undertakes <b>radical and partial nephrectomy</b>, <b>radical cystectomy</b>, <b>orchiectomy</b>, and <b>penectomy</b> for urological malignancies. Reconstructive procedures such as <b>hypospadias repair</b>, <b>ureteric reimplantation</b>, and <b>bladder augmentation</b> are also performed.<o:p></o:p></font></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: normal;"><b><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana"><u>Andrology and Other Procedures<o:p></o:p></u></font></b></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: normal;"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana">The unit also manages <b>male infertility</b>, <b>varicocele ligation</b>, <b>hydrocele excision</b>, and <b>vasectomy</b>services. Endoscopic evaluation, including <b>diagnostic cystoscopy</b> and <b>retrograde pyelography</b>, are regularly undertaken.<o:p></o:p></font></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: normal;"><b><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana"><u>Clinical and Academic Focus</u><o:p></o:p></font></b></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: normal;"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana">The Urology Unit emphasizes patient-centered care, early diagnosis, and minimally invasive treatment. Regular <b>academic sessions</b>, <b>case discussions</b>, and <b>collaboration with nephrology and radiology</b> ensure comprehensive management. The team also contributes actively to research and surgical skill training.<o:p></o:p></font></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: normal;"><b><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana"><u>Breast Surgery</u></font></b></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: normal;"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana">Comprehensive management of benign and malignant breast conditions is offered, supported by dedicated diagnostic facilities including mammography, ultrasonography, and FNAC/core biopsy.<br>Common and advanced surgical procedures performed include:<o:p></o:p></font></p> <ul type="disc" style=""> <li class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;      line-height:normal;mso-list:l1 level1 lfo5;tab-stops:list 36.0pt"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana"><b>Breast lump excision and fibroadenoma surgery</b><o:p></o:p></font></li> <li class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;      line-height:normal;mso-list:l1 level1 lfo5;tab-stops:list 36.0pt"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana"><b>Modified Radical Mastectomy (MRM)</b> and <b>Simple Mastectomy</b><o:p></o:p></font></li> <li class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;      line-height:normal;mso-list:l1 level1 lfo5;tab-stops:list 36.0pt"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana"><b>Breast-Conserving Surgery (BCS)</b> for early breast carcinoma<o:p></o:p></font></li> <li class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;      line-height:normal;mso-list:l1 level1 lfo5;tab-stops:list 36.0pt"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana"><b>Sentinel Lymph Node Biopsy (SLNB)</b> and <b>Axillary Dissection</b><o:p></o:p></font></li> <li class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;      line-height:normal;mso-list:l1 level1 lfo5;tab-stops:list 36.0pt"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana"><b>Oncoplastic reconstruction</b> for aesthetic and functional restoration      after cancer surgery<o:p></o:p></font></li> <li class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;      line-height:normal;mso-list:l1 level1 lfo5;tab-stops:list 36.0pt"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana"><b>Incision and drainage</b> for abscesses and infections<o:p></o:p></font></li></ul> <p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: normal;"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana">The unit follows a <b>multidisciplinary oncology model</b>, involving coordination with radiology, pathology, and medical oncology for diagnosis, staging, and postoperative management. Early detection and patient education remain core components of breast care services.<o:p></o:p></font></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: normal;"><b><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana"><u>Endocrine Surgery</u><o:p></o:p></font></b></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: normal;"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana">The endocrine division provides surgical treatment for a variety of thyroid and parathyroid disorders, supported by hormone assays, ultrasonography, and FNAC facilities.<br>Key procedures include:<o:p></o:p></font></p> <ul type="disc" style=""> <li class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;      line-height:normal;mso-list:l7 level1 lfo6;tab-stops:list 36.0pt"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana"><b>Hemithyroidectomy</b> and <b>Total Thyroidectomy</b> for benign and      malignant thyroid diseases<o:p></o:p></font></li> <li class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;      line-height:normal;mso-list:l7 level1 lfo6;tab-stops:list 36.0pt"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana"><b>Completion Thyroidectomy</b> for residual thyroid carcinoma<o:p></o:p></font></li> <li class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;      line-height:normal;mso-list:l7 level1 lfo6;tab-stops:list 36.0pt"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana"><b>Parathyroidectomy</b> for hyperparathyroidism<o:p></o:p></font></li> <li class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;      line-height:normal;mso-list:l7 level1 lfo6;tab-stops:list 36.0pt"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana"><b>Adrenalectomy</b> (open and laparoscopic) for adrenal tumours      and functional adenomas<o:p></o:p></font></li></ul> <p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: normal;"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana">All procedures are performed with strict adherence to safety protocols, intraoperative nerve monitoring (where indicated), and a focus on preserving gland function and minimizing complications.<o:p></o:p></font></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: normal;"><span style="font-family: Verdana; font-size: small;">The Breast and Endocrine Unit conducts regular </span><b style="font-family: Verdana; font-size: small;">case discussions</b><span style="font-family: Verdana; font-size: small;">, </span><b style="font-family: Verdana; font-size: small;">tumour board meetings</b><span style="font-family: Verdana; font-size: small;">, and </span><b style="font-family: Verdana; font-size: small;">morbidity-mortality audits</b><span style="font-family: Verdana; font-size: small;"> to ensure continuous clinical improvement. Emphasis is placed on </span><b style="font-family: Verdana; font-size: small;">early diagnosis, organ preservation</b><span style="font-family: Verdana; font-size: small;">, and </span><b style="font-family: Verdana; font-size: small;">comprehensive postoperative follow-up</b><span style="font-family: Verdana; font-size: small;">.</span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: normal;"><b><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana"><u>Plastic and Reconstructive Surgery</u><o:p></o:p></font></b></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: normal;"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana">This unit handles <b>post-traumatic reconstruction</b>, <b>burn management</b>, <b>skin grafting</b>, <b>flap cover for soft tissue defects</b>, <b>microsurgical procedures</b>, and <b>cosmetic surgeries</b>. It plays a vital role in multidisciplinary care for trauma and oncology patients.<o:p></o:p></font></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: normal;"><b><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana"><u>Pediatric Surgery</u><o:p></o:p></font></b></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: normal;"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana">Specialized care is provided for <b>congenital anomalies</b>, <b>pediatric hernia and hydrocele repair</b>, <b>hypospadias correction</b>, <b>pediatric appendectomy</b>, and <b>urological reconstructive procedures</b>. Neonatal and infant surgeries are performed with a focus on safety and precision.<o:p></o:p></font></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: normal;"><b><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana"><u>Vascular Surgery</u><o:p></o:p></font></b></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: normal;"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana">Services include <b>varicose vein surgery</b>, <b>arteriovenous fistula creation for dialysis</b>, <b>embolectomy</b>, <b>bypass and repair procedures for peripheral vascular disease</b>, and <b>wound management for ischemic limbs</b>.<o:p></o:p></font></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: normal;"><b><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana"><u>Colo-proctology</u></font></b></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: normal;"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana">This section performs <b>hemorrhoidectomy</b>, <b>fistulotomy/fistulectomy</b>, <b>fissure surgery</b>, <b>laparoscopic colorectal resections</b>, and <b>pilonidal sinus excision</b>. Modern modalities like <b>stapler hemorrhoidopexy</b> and <b>laser proctology</b> are available.<o:p></o:p></font></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: normal;"><b><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana"><u>Surgical Oncology</u><o:p></o:p></font></b></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: normal;"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana">Comprehensive cancer surgeries including <b>breast, thyroid, colorectal, gastrointestinal, and soft tissue malignancies</b> are undertaken with a multidisciplinary approach. The focus remains on curative resections, organ preservation, and patient rehabilitation.<o:p></o:p></font></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: normal;"><span style="font-family: Verdana; font-size: small;">The </span><b style="font-family: Verdana; font-size: small;">Department of Surgery</b><span style="font-family: Verdana; font-size: small;"> at </span><b style="font-family: Verdana; font-size: small;">Northern Railways Central Hospital (NRCH)</b><span style="font-family: Verdana; font-size: small;"> is staffed by a team of highly qualified and experienced </span><b style="font-family: Verdana; font-size: small;">faculty members and senior residents</b><span style="font-family: Verdana; font-size: small;"> who form the backbone of surgical services in the institution. The department is known for its commitment to clinical excellence, patient-centered care, and academic advancement.</span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: normal;"><b><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana"><u>Faculty</u><o:p></o:p></font></b></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: normal;"><span style="font-family: Verdana; font-size: small;">1.</span><b style="font-family: Verdana; font-size: small;">Dr.(Prof) Biswanath Tiwary , head of department</b><span style="font-family: Verdana; font-size: small;"> with vast experience across various surgical subspecialties, including </span><b style="font-family: Verdana; font-size: small;">General Surgery,&nbsp; Gastrointestinal and HPB Surgery, Breast and Endocrine Surgery Coloproctology, and Surgical Oncology</b><span style="font-family: Verdana; font-size: small;">.</span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: normal;"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana">2. <b>Dr.(Prof) Sanjeev Singhal,</b> having a vast experience of 33 years<o:p></o:p></font></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: normal;"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana">3.<b> Dr.(Prof) Pawan Malik<o:p></o:p></b></font></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: normal;"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana"><b>4. Dr.(Asst. Prof) Vashishth Rai</b><o:p></o:p></font></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: normal;"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana"><br>Their responsibilities include:<o:p></o:p></font></p> <ul type="disc" style=""> <li class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;      line-height:normal;mso-list:l8 level1 lfo7;tab-stops:list 36.0pt"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana">Performing elective and emergency surgeries.<o:p></o:p></font></li> <li class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;      line-height:normal;mso-list:l8 level1 lfo7;tab-stops:list 36.0pt"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana">Supervising OPD, ward, and OT services.<o:p></o:p></font></li> <li class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;      line-height:normal;mso-list:l8 level1 lfo7;tab-stops:list 36.0pt"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana">Conducting teaching sessions, case      discussions, and surgical skill training.<o:p></o:p></font></li> <li class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;      line-height:normal;mso-list:l8 level1 lfo7;tab-stops:list 36.0pt"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana">Guiding research activities, publications, and      academic audits.<o:p></o:p></font></li> <li class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;      line-height:normal;mso-list:l8 level1 lfo7;tab-stops:list 36.0pt"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana">Participating in multidisciplinary team      meetings for comprehensive patient management.<o:p></o:p></font></li></ul> <p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: normal;"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana">The faculty members also contribute actively to hospital administration, surgical protocol development, and quality assurance initiatives, ensuring adherence to the highest standards of care.<o:p></o:p></font></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: normal;"><b><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana"><u>Senior Residents</u><o:p></o:p></font></b></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: normal;"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana">The <b>Senior Residents</b>play a vital role in maintaining round-the-clock surgical services. They are responsible for:<o:p></o:p></font></p> <ul type="disc" style=""> <li class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;      line-height:normal;mso-list:l6 level1 lfo8;tab-stops:list 36.0pt"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana">Conducting daily ward rounds, preoperative      preparation, and postoperative management.<o:p></o:p></font></li> <li class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;      line-height:normal;mso-list:l6 level1 lfo8;tab-stops:list 36.0pt"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana">Managing OPD and emergency cases.<o:p></o:p></font></li> <li class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;      line-height:normal;mso-list:l6 level1 lfo8;tab-stops:list 36.0pt"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana">Assisting and performing surgeries under      supervision.<o:p></o:p></font></li> <li class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;      line-height:normal;mso-list:l6 level1 lfo8;tab-stops:list 36.0pt"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana">Participating in academic activities such as      seminars, audits, and morbidity-mortality meetings.<o:p></o:p></font></li> <li class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;      line-height:normal;mso-list:l6 level1 lfo8;tab-stops:list 36.0pt"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana">Coordinating with other departments for      multidisciplinary patient care.<o:p></o:p></font></li></ul> <p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: normal;"><font class="font_12px" style="color:black;" size="2" face="Verdana">Their rigorous clinical training ensures the development of surgical competence, decision-making skills, and professionalism, preparing them for independent surgical practice in the future.</font><span style="font-family: " times="" new="" roman",="" serif;="" font-size:="" 12pt;"=""><o:p></o:p></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 12px; line-height: normal;"><img src="https://nr.indianrailways.gov.in//uploads/images/1754223734697-Surgery Schedule.png"></p></div><span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 12px;"><img src="https://nr.indianrailways.gov.in//uploads/images/1754545165534-Surgery Special Clinics.png"></span><br></div><p></p>
